=== ENVIRONMENTAL / PRE-EXISTING GATE LIMITATIONS (NOT this surface) ===
================================================================================
The four non-zero whole-gate steps are caused entirely by pre-existing sibling
state and a runner-capability gap. This surface contributes ZERO errors and ZERO
violations to all of them (greps below run against the actual gate logs):

[1] iOS build test = 65  ->  pre-existing parallel-merge type collisions.
    The committed tree's iOS app target does not compile: 717 `error:` lines, of which
    0 reference BackupMonitorWidget. Dominant cause: `DashboardWidgetSize` is declared
    `public struct` in 15+ sibling widget files (2 in committed Sources/DashboardWidgets,
    13+ in TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/*Widget.Model.swift), so it is "ambiguous for type
    lookup" everywhere (294 occurrences), plus other duplicated sibling models
    (PowerFlowConnection, VehicleHeroModel, ChargingSessionSummary, ...). This surface uses
    its OWN `BackupMonitorGridSize` (the DigitalTwinMini pattern) and references none of the
    ambiguous types.  grep "error:" ios_final.log | grep -c BackupMonitor  ->  0

[2] macOS build test = 65  ->  runner lacks a macOS development signing certificate.
    Build halts BEFORE Swift compilation at:
      "'TeslaSync-macOS' has entitlements that require signing with a development
       certificate. Enable development signing in the Signing & Capabilities editor."
    (also TeslaSyncWidgets-macOS). 0 compile errors, 0 in this surface. This is the SAME
    block the accepted sibling logs documented (p4-...-0049-ExportStatusWidget: "macos
    test-host-signing(no-dev-cert)"; p4-...-0035-DigitalTwinMiniWidget).

[3] swiftlint --strict (whole tree) = 2  ->  sibling-only.
    Only violation: TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/LifetimeStatsWidget.Adapter.swift:141
    function_body_length. 0 violations in BackupMonitorWidget.*.

[4] swiftformat --lint apps/apple = 1  ->  sibling-only.
    "1/1920 files require formatting" — an unrelated sibling file. 0 in BackupMonitorWidget.*.

These are pre-existing across the ~440 parallel-merge branches in this tree (HEAD
c9c6fdb9f); they are integration/runner conditions, not surface defects. To make the
APP TARGET buildable at all (so the surface and its tests can be hosted), project.yml was
given an `excludes: ["*Tests.swift","**/*Tests.swift"]` on the iOS+macOS app targets'
dashboard-widgets/feature-views source groups (262 co-located *Tests.swift files were being
compiled into the app target and failed `import XCTest`), and this surface's co-located
BackupMonitorWidget.Tests.swift was wired into TeslaSyncTests + TeslaSync-macOSTests. This
mirrors the accepted DigitalTwinMini precedent, which also committed project.yml.

